id: pm-graph-g8uc
title: Remove vulnerable braces dependency from certification toolchain
description: pm-ops 2026.10.4 and direct fast-glob 3.3.3 depend on micromatch 4.0.8 / braces 3.0.3. Full npm audit flags GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm (stack exhaustion). npm view braces version returns 3.0.3; braces@3.0.4 is E404. Require published compatible fix or independently tested safe replacement; do not downgrade required pm-ops pin or suppress audit.
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-04T11:00:37.158Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-04T14:13:52.131Z"
author: codex-sol
severity: high
expected_result: npm audit reports zero vulnerabilities with PM 2026.10.4 pins.
actual_result: "Removal experiment: full audit zero, but canonical duplication cannot load its fast-glob optional peer (ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND). pm-ops2026.10.4 declares fast-glob^3.3.3 in peerDependencies with optional:true; restored exact3.3.3 for the required consumer gate. Full audit4high remains; no compatible patched braces3 release or gate exception."
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-04T14:13:51.136Z",codex-sol,"Correction after complete installed manifest inspection: pm-ops2026.10.4 DOES declare fast-glob^3.3.3 as an optional peer, not a direct dependency. The earlier undeclared-import wording was inaccurate; its duplication entrypoint statically imports that peer, so a duplication consumer must supply it. The removal experiment still proved clean audit plus broken canonical duplication, then restoring exact3.3.3 preserved the gate. This is an unresolved vulnerable optional-peer chain, not a proven missing-declaration upstream defect. Full development audit4high remains the blocker; prod audit0 and full functional gates are unchanged."
files[2]{path,scope}:
  package-lock.json,project
  package.json,project
body: ""
